1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,050
Last time, we learnt that an iron nail can be magnetised by

2
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:05,170
the stroke method.

3
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:08,900
Only a magnetic object can be made into a magnet.

4
00:00:11,013 --> 00:00:13,343
A little ant is hiding in this video.

5
00:00:13,593 --> 00:00:14,833
Can you spot it?

6
00:00:14,958 --> 00:00:16,798
Lock in first with your fingers.

7
00:00:17,068 --> 00:00:18,898
One finger for every point.

8
00:00:19,485 --> 00:00:20,785
Today you'll learn:

9
00:00:20,989 --> 00:00:22,329
One way, one pole.

10
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:24,000
The same pole.

11
00:00:24,205 --> 00:00:25,865
More strokes, stronger.

12
00:00:27,469 --> 00:00:28,349
Round one.

13
00:00:28,659 --> 00:00:31,969
Basil rubbed his nail back and forth, with both ends of the

14
00:00:31,989 --> 00:00:32,779
magnet.

15
00:00:33,029 --> 00:00:36,219
Pip stroked his one way, with one pole, the same number of

16
00:00:36,239 --> 00:00:37,039
times.

17
00:00:37,309 --> 00:00:39,529
Which nail attracts more steel clips?

18
00:00:39,829 --> 00:00:40,999
One, Basil's.

19
00:00:41,289 --> 00:00:42,249
Two, Pip's.

20
00:00:42,529 --> 00:00:43,959
Three, both the same.

21
00:00:44,249 --> 00:00:45,599
Show me your fingers.

22
00:00:51,074 --> 00:00:52,054
Locked in!

23
00:00:52,182 --> 00:00:52,812
One!

24
00:00:52,942 --> 00:00:54,872
Back and forth is twice the rubbing.

25
00:00:54,982 --> 00:00:56,882
So my nail is twice as strong!

26
00:00:56,932 --> 00:01:01,482
Two. I lifted the magnet away after every stroke, so I never rubbed

27
00:01:01,502 --> 00:01:02,642
it the wrong way.

28
00:01:02,697 --> 00:01:03,437
Two!

29
00:01:03,557 --> 00:01:07,367
Rubbing back, or with the other end, can undo the stroke before.

30
00:01:07,639 --> 00:01:09,159
Be a steel paper clip!

31
00:01:09,419 --> 00:01:10,419
Shrink down.

32
00:01:10,699 --> 00:01:11,629
Quietly.

33
00:01:13,912 --> 00:01:16,752
You are a steel paper clip, lying in a tray with your

34
00:01:16,772 --> 00:01:17,602
friends.

35
00:01:18,392 --> 00:01:20,802
A giant nail comes down from above.

36
00:01:21,314 --> 00:01:22,774
It is Basil's nail.

37
00:01:23,584 --> 00:01:26,074
You wobble a little, and then you lie still.

38
00:01:26,844 --> 00:01:28,514
It hardly pulls you at all.

39
00:01:29,028 --> 00:01:30,548
Here comes Pip's nail.

40
00:01:31,328 --> 00:01:33,658
You slide, you tip up, and you jump!

41
00:01:34,448 --> 00:01:37,378
You cling to its tip, and a friend clings to you!

42
00:01:39,033 --> 00:01:41,143
The answer is two: Pip's nail!

43
00:01:41,393 --> 00:01:42,973
Did you show two fingers?

44
00:01:43,243 --> 00:01:44,612
Put one finger up!

45
00:01:44,632 --> 00:01:48,012
Pip's strokes all went the same way, so every stroke helped.

46
00:01:48,222 --> 00:01:50,703
Basil's back and forth undid his own work!

47
00:01:50,723 --> 00:01:52,973
So how do I get back to the head of the nail,

48
00:01:52,993 --> 00:01:54,993
without rubbing it the wrong way?

49
00:01:55,647 --> 00:01:56,797
Look closer.

50
00:01:57,357 --> 00:02:00,277
Put one pole of the magnet on the head of the nail.

51
00:02:00,877 --> 00:02:02,737
Slide it all the way to the tip.

52
00:02:02,757 --> 00:02:05,707
Then lift it up and away, in a big curve, back to

53
00:02:05,727 --> 00:02:06,407
the head.

54
00:02:06,987 --> 00:02:09,079
Never slide it back along the nail.

55
00:02:09,099 --> 00:02:12,359
Stroke after stroke, the magnet moves the same way.

56
00:02:12,379 --> 00:02:15,989
Same direction means the same way every time, such as from the

57
00:02:16,009 --> 00:02:19,119
head of the nail to its tip, stroke after stroke!

58
00:02:22,421 --> 00:02:23,641
Say it with me!

59
00:02:24,355 --> 00:02:27,715
Stroke the iron nail with one pole of a bar magnet.

60
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:31,285
Repeat the strokes in the same direction each time.

61
00:02:34,765 --> 00:02:35,665
Showdown!

62
00:02:35,975 --> 00:02:37,105
Double points.

63
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:40,525
Pip's poster for the class party has one mistake.

64
00:02:40,805 --> 00:02:42,585
Line one, two, or three?

65
00:02:42,875 --> 00:02:44,345
Show me with your fingers.

66
00:02:44,407 --> 00:02:47,397
One: stroke from the head to the tip, with the red end.

67
00:02:47,547 --> 00:02:50,197
Two: lift the magnet away, back to the head.

68
00:02:50,437 --> 00:02:53,897
Three: halfway, turn the magnet round and use the blue end too,

69
00:02:53,917 --> 00:02:55,007
for more strength.

70
00:03:00,618 --> 00:03:01,598
Locked in!

71
00:03:01,726 --> 00:03:02,426
Three!

72
00:03:02,576 --> 00:03:05,916
Switching to the other end undoes the strokes, just like my back

73
00:03:05,936 --> 00:03:07,056
and forth did.

74
00:03:07,932 --> 00:03:09,022
Three fingers?

75
00:03:09,262 --> 00:03:11,192
Put up two more on your score hand!

76
00:03:11,327 --> 00:03:15,067
Same pole means the same end of the magnet every time, such

77
00:03:15,087 --> 00:03:18,097
as the red North pole, for every single stroke!

78
00:03:18,608 --> 00:03:21,568
Make sure to stroke the iron nail with the same pole.

79
00:03:22,533 --> 00:03:24,893
Our big fish has two clips on its nose.

80
00:03:24,933 --> 00:03:27,493
How do we make a hook strong enough to catch it?

81
00:03:28,144 --> 00:03:29,294
Look closer.

82
00:03:29,874 --> 00:03:34,235
Three new nails, all the same, get ten, twenty and thirty strokes.

83
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:35,735
Put the magnet away.

84
00:03:36,335 --> 00:03:38,805
Then dip each nail into the steel clips.

85
00:03:38,825 --> 00:03:42,538
The more strokes a nail gets, the more steel clips it attracts.

86
00:03:42,558 --> 00:03:46,568
A stronger magnet is a magnet that attracts more steel clips, such

87
00:03:46,588 --> 00:03:48,488
as the nail with thirty strokes!

88
00:03:54,993 --> 00:03:56,153
Say it with me!

89
00:03:56,862 --> 00:04:00,152
The iron nail will become a stronger magnet when it is stroked

90
00:04:00,172 --> 00:04:02,032
more times with the magnet.

91
00:04:04,797 --> 00:04:05,902
Say it with us!

92
00:04:06,562 --> 00:04:07,532
Which way?

93
00:04:08,142 --> 00:04:09,506
The same direction!

94
00:04:12,962 --> 00:04:13,936
Which end?

95
00:04:14,542 --> 00:04:15,737
The same pole!

96
00:04:19,362 --> 00:04:20,507
More strokes?

97
00:04:20,942 --> 00:04:22,339
A stronger magnet!

98
00:04:26,517 --> 00:04:27,977
Show me your score hand!

99
00:04:28,257 --> 00:04:29,707
Two fingers or more?

100
00:04:29,997 --> 00:04:31,357
You beat the Buddies.

101
00:04:31,647 --> 00:04:32,717
Three fingers?

102
00:04:32,997 --> 00:04:33,997
High five!

103
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,600
Did you spot the ant?

104
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:38,410
It was on the edge of the sink, leading a little line

105
00:04:38,430 --> 00:04:39,250
of ants!

106
00:04:39,385 --> 00:04:40,685
Here is a fun fact!

107
00:04:40,755 --> 00:04:43,655
When an ant finds food, it leaves a smell path on its

108
00:04:43,675 --> 00:04:44,535
way home.

109
00:04:44,825 --> 00:04:47,975
More ants follow the same path, again and again, and the smell

110
00:04:47,995 --> 00:04:49,175
gets stronger!

111
00:04:49,299 --> 00:04:50,579
Tell someone at home!

112
00:04:51,518 --> 00:04:55,708
Next time: Momo coils a long wire round a new iron nail,

113
00:04:55,798 --> 00:04:57,978
and joins its two ends to a battery.

114
00:04:58,238 --> 00:05:00,598
The nail attracts some steel paper clips.

115
00:05:00,868 --> 00:05:02,748
Then she takes the battery away.

116
00:05:03,008 --> 00:05:04,598
What happens to the clips?

117
00:05:04,868 --> 00:05:06,468
One, they stay on the nail.

118
00:05:06,758 --> 00:05:08,118
Two, they drop off.

119
00:05:08,388 --> 00:05:09,708
Lock in your answer!

120
00:05:09,985 --> 00:05:12,185
Let's read today's key words together!

121
00:05:12,475 --> 00:05:13,235
Ready?

122
00:05:13,522 --> 00:05:14,752
Same direction.

123
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:17,460
Same pole.

124
00:05:18,968 --> 00:05:20,258
Stronger magnet.

125
00:05:21,961 --> 00:05:22,901
Well done!

126
00:05:23,883 --> 00:05:24,984
Say it with us!

127
00:05:25,784 --> 00:05:26,534
Ready?

128
00:05:26,658 --> 00:05:27,318
One!

129
00:05:27,658 --> 00:05:28,358
two!

130
00:05:28,663 --> 00:05:29,838
Now you know!
